Third-party notices
===================

This image is an aggregation of separately licensed programs. Nothing here is
statically linked into anything else: OBS, GStreamer and Selkies are separate
processes started by runtime-init, which is Gleem's own code.

Where the licences are
----------------------

Every Debian package in this image carries its own licence at
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright. `dpkg-query -W` lists what is
installed.

OBS Studio is not a Debian package: Debian builds it without the browser
source, so the image builds OBS itself.

  /usr/bin/obs and   OBS Studio, GPL-2.0-or-later
  /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libobs*, obs-plugins/, /usr/share/obs
                     licence at /usr/share/doc/obs-studio/COPYING

It is built unmodified from https://github.com/obsproject/obs-studio at the
release commit the Containerfile pins (OBS_COMMIT), submodules included. That
repository at that commit is its complete corresponding source.

The browser source runs on the Chromium Embedded Framework, which OBS
distributes as a prebuilt binary and the image takes unmodified from OBS's own
download server, checked against the hash OBS publishes for that release:

  obs-plugins/libcef.so and the files beside it
                     CEF, BSD-3-Clause, bundling Chromium and its third-party
                     components under their own licences
                     licence at /usr/share/doc/obs-studio/cef/LICENSE.txt,
                     version at /usr/share/doc/obs-studio/cef/README.txt

Two payloads are not Debian packages and are therefore called out here:

  /opt/selkies       Selkies, MPL-2.0     licence at /usr/share/doc/selkies/LICENSE
  /opt/selkies-web   Selkies, MPL-2.0     licence at /opt/selkies-web/LICENSE

One OBS plugin is not a Debian package either:

  obs-irl-control    OBS IRL Control, GPL-2.0-or-later
                     /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/obs-plugins/obs-irl-control.so
                     licence at /usr/share/doc/obs-irl-control/LICENSE

It is built from source in the image build, from the public repository
https://github.com/gleem-gg/obs-irl-control at the commit the Containerfile
pins (IRL_CONTROL_COMMIT). That repository is its complete corresponding
