Modifying anything here
-----------------------

MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: a modified Selkies file must stay MPL-2.0 and
its source must be made available. That is the whole obligation — it does not
reach Gleem's own files, even in the same image. Files are kept byte-identical
to upstream precisely so this stays a non-issue; see the note in the vendored
web client's README.

Patching OBS, GStreamer or any other GPL component and shipping the result
would put those changes under the GPL and require publishing them. Nothing in
this image is patched today.
